SECTION 1 — WHY THIS SPRINT EXISTS
==========================================================================

A `/graphify` run on `apps/dashboard/src` (2026-05-12) produced:
1289 nodes · 3178 edges · 69 communities · 99% EXTRACTED edges.

The graph surfaces three classes of fragility:

1. `lib/utils.ts` is the #1 god leaf (`cn()` has 251 in-edges, the file
   has 70 importers). Any helper added here inherits the full importer
   set — safe today, brittle as the codebase grows.

2. `components/fields/` and `components/content-toolbar/` are *feature
   shaped folders* living inside `components/`. They own domain logic
   (`registry.ts`, `FilterOperator`, `Seed`, `Branch`) but bypass the
   VSA contract that reserves `components/` for stateless primitives.
   `components/content-toolbar/index.ts` is also a `export *` barrel,
   which makes every internal symbol public by accident.

3. Three concrete cross-slice import inversions:
   - `features/content-management/hooks/use-content-facets.ts` and
     `use-content-item.ts` import `DASHBOARD_QUERY_KEYS` from
     `@/features/dashboard`. Content depends on dashboard — wrong way.
   - `components/ui/date-picker-input.tsx` imports
     `useGeneralSettings` from `@/features/settings/hooks/use-settings`.
     A UI primitive must not read slice state directly.
   - `pages/widget-lab.tsx` imports widgets from
     `@/features/dashboard/components/widgets` (deep path) instead of
     the public barrel.

Plus four import cycles inside `components/ui/minimal-tiptap/`,
documented by the graph, that block tree-shaking on the editor module.

